# Dart Coding Standards

Aligned with `analysis_options.yaml` (`flutter_lints` + project overrides).

## Style

- Prefer **single quotes** (`prefer_single_quotes`).
- Prefer `final` locals/fields; prefer `const` where possible.
- Prefer **relative imports** inside `lib/` (`prefer_relative_imports`).
- No `print` — use `Logger` from `lib/core/utils/logger.dart`.
- Keep lines ≤ ~80 characters; use trailing commas.
- Prefer expression bodies / arrow syntax for one-liners.
- No empty catch blocks.

## Naming

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Files | snake_case | `home_repository_impl.dart` |
| Classes | PascalCase | `HomeRepositoryImpl` |
| Private members | `_` prefix | `_products` |
| Booleans | auxiliary verb | `isLoading`, `hasReachedMax` |
| Routes | `RouteNames.k{Name}Page` | `kCartPage` |
| DI init | `init{Feature}()` | `initHome()` |
| Use cases | `Get{Entity}UseCase` | `GetProductUseCase` |

## Patterns in use

- Entities/`Equatable` for value equality.
- Manual `fromJson`/`toJson` on models (no json_serializable).
- Cubit states: abstract base + `Initial` / `Loading` / `Loaded` / `Error` subclasses (not Freezed).
- Mixins: `CancelableSafeCubitMixin` for cancelable async cubits.

## Avoid

- Freezed / sealed codegen for states unless user requests.
- Package imports for files under `lib/` when relative works.
- Editing generated `*.g.dart` by hand.
